    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Why this dashboard exists",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Everything on **Service Health** describes a failure a normal web service can also have: it is down, it is erroring, it is slow.\n\nThe gap on the left describes a failure with **none of those symptoms**. When `FairnessGapExceeded` fires, `up` is 1, the error ratio is 0, p95 latency is inside budget and every request returns 200. Every panel an ordinary on-call rotation looks at is green — and the system is treating men and women differently in who gets called by the collections team.\n\nThat is the whole argument for ML-specific observability, and it escalates to compliance, not to the on-call engineer. There is nothing to restart."
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
